{
  "configuration_id": "config_005",
  "reason": "The sole data point (config_018: multimodal/multiprofile/scvi_n200/resnet50/avgpool/weighted → 0.678 acc) establishes a baseline but leaves the impact of the image encoder completely untested. Config_005 is a minimal, controlled change: it swaps resnet50 for imagenet_vit_l while holding every other variable (multimodal, multiprofile, scvi_n200, avgpool, weighted) constant. This directly tests whether a substantially more powerful image backbone can push accuracy higher, which is likely the single largest lever available. If ViT-L yields a clear gain, it re-centers the search around a stronger image encoder; if it does not, we learn ResNet50 is sufficient and can redirect effort toward RNA encoder, aggregation, or fusion choices. With 8 experiments remaining, this clean A/B comparison maximizes information per trial and avoids prematurely committing to a suboptimal image backbone."
}

